  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "In {recent} years, researchers from {diverse} fields have agreed that short-termism is now a significant problem in {industrialized} {societies} .The immediate gratification {fever} has infected everything from {capital} markets to {private} life, causing some of the world's most serious problems: {climate} change, {biodiversity} collapse, and more.The {historian} Francis Cole argues that the West has entered a {period} where “only the present {exists} , a present characterized at once by the {cruelty} of the instant and by the boredom of an {unending} now”.",
      "cn": "<u> 近 </u> 年来， <u> 不同 </u> 领域的研究人员一致认为，只注重短期效益的思维方式现在已成为 <u> 工业化社会 </u> 的一个重大问题。急功近利的 <u> 热潮 </u> 已经影响了社会的方方面面，从 <u> 资本 </u> 市场到 <u> 私人 </u> 生活，造成了一些世界上最严重的问题： <u> 气候 </u> 变化、 <u> 生物多样性 </u> 崩溃等等。 <u> 历史学家 </u> 弗朗西斯·科尔认为，西方社会已经进入了一个 <u> 时期 </u> ，此时“只有当下 <u> 存在 </u> ，而这个当下的特点在于瞬间的 <u> 残酷无情 </u> 和对 <u> 无尽的 </u> 现在的厌倦”。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "It has been proved that people have a bias ( (偏向) ) towards the present, focusing on loud {attractions} in the moment at the {expense} of health, well-being and financial stability of their future {selves} or community.We use disposable {tissues} and plastic chopsticks for the immediate convenience despite the problems they cause.In business, this bias {surfaces} as {short-sighted} decisions.And on slow-burning problems like climate change, it translates into the unwillingness to make small sacrifices ( (牺牲) ) today that could make a major difference {tomorrow} .Instead, the {premier} concern is next {quarter's profit} , or a deadline in {September} .As a result, the construction of new {housing} projects and {ports} may receive more attention than the conservation of forests and wetlands.",
      "cn": "事实证明，人们对当下存在一种偏向，只专注于当下那些 <u> 引人注目的事物 </u> ，却 <u> 牺牲 </u> 了未来 <u> 自己 </u> 以及所在社区的健康、幸福和财务稳定。我们使用一次性 <u> 纸巾 </u> 和塑料筷子，只图一时的方便，全然不顾它们造成的问题。在商业领域，这种偏向 <u> 表现 </u> 为 <u> 目光短浅的 </u> 决策。而在气候变化这类缓慢发展的问题上，这种偏向则表现为，人们不情愿在当下做出微小的牺牲，即使这些牺牲可能会在 <u> 明天 </u> 带来重大的改变。相反，人们关心的 <u> 首要 </u> 问题是下个 <u> 季度 </u> 的 <u> 利润 </u> ，或 <u> 9月份 </u> 的某个截止日期。因此，新的 <u> 住房 </u> 项目和 <u> 港口 </u> 建设可能比保护森林和湿地更受重视。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "These {biased} perspectives cannot be {blamed} on one single cause.It is {fair} to say, though, that our {psychological} biases play a major role.People's {hesitancy} to {delay} satisfaction is the most obvious example.Think of how a quick {discount} has urged you to purchase.But there are other biases to be {mentioned} .One of them is about how the most {accessible} information in the present affects decisions about the future.For instance, you might hear someone say:“It's cold this {winter} , so I needn't {worry} about global {warming} .”Another is that loud and urgent matters are given too much importance, making people ignore longer-term trends that {arguably} matter more.This is when a {pop} star's new {hit} draws far more attention than, say, the {twin} crises of climate change and {gradual} biodiversity decline.",
      "cn": "这些 <u> 有偏见的 </u> 观点不能被 <u> 归咎 </u> 于单一的原因。不过， <u> 恰当 </u> 地说，我们的 <u> 心理 </u> 偏见起到了重要的作用。人们 <u> 不愿延迟 </u> 获得满足感就是最明显的例子。想想看，那些限时 <u> 折扣 </u> 是如何促使你买东西的。不过，其他的偏见同样值得一 <u> 提 </u> 。其中之一是当前最 <u> 容易获得的 </u> 信息如何影响我们对未来的决策。例如，你可能听到某个人说：“今年 <u> 冬天 </u> 很冷，所以我不需要 <u> 担心 </u> 全球 <u> 变暖 </u> 的问题。”另一种偏见是，那些声势浩大的、紧迫的事情被过度重视，导致人们忽视了 <u> 按理来说 </u> 更为重要的长期趋势。这就好比一位 <u> 流行 </u> 歌星的新 <u> 热门歌曲 </u> 会比气候变化和生物多样性 <u> 逐渐 </u> 减少这 <u> 两 </u> 大危机吸引更多的关注。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "As a psychologist once joked, if aliens ( (外星人) ) wanted to {weaken} {humanity} , they wouldn't send {ships} ; they would {invent} climate change.Indeed, when it comes to environmental {transformations} , we can develop a form of {collective} “ {poor} memory”，and each new generation can believe the state of {affairs} they encounter is nothing out of the ordinary.Older people today, for example, can remember a time with insect-covered car {windscreens} after long drives.Children, on the other hand, have no idea that insect {population} has dropped dramatically.",
      "cn": "正如一位心理学家曾开过的玩笑：如果外星人想 <u> 削弱人类 </u> ，他们不会派 <u> 飞船 </u> 来，而是会 <u> 发明 </u> 气候变化。的确，在环境 <u> 变化 </u> 方面，我们会形成一种“记忆力 <u> 欠佳 </u> ”的 <u> 集体性 </u> 趋势，每一代人都会认为自己所遇到的 <u> 状况 </u> 并不稀奇。例如，如今的老年人还记得这样一段时光：过去长途驾驶后，汽车 <u> 挡风玻璃 </u> 上会布满昆虫。而另一方面，孩子们根本不知道，昆虫的 <u> 数量 </u> 已经急剧下降了。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP4m+378Hw1xTRxUdPaP/PFjKUFq4K2G7tp6ZLYoCE601yW1W39VMdLmovFdSHs4nVQ=="
    }
  ],
